  ( TransactionDb :> es
  , Error ServerError :> es
  ) =>
  UUID ->
  Eff es Sale.SaleTransaction
  ! early 409 'Only an open sale can be cleared' unless the loaded sale is Created or InProgress; then clearSale, which re-checks under the lock; a refusal goes through Service.Transaction.refuseWrite
  ! returns the emptied sale, whose status is Created
  ! emits no event and does not cancel stock pulls
  ~ called by: Server.SaleCommand.saleCommandServer
  ? tested by: Test.Service.SaleSpec.spec

finalize ::
  ( TransactionDb :> es
  , EventEmitter :> es
  , Clock :> es
  , Error ServerError :> es
  ) =>
  UUID ->
  Eff es Sale.SaleTransaction
  ! is Service.Transaction.finalizeTx and nothing more. The checks for no lines and for short payment moved into DB.Transaction.finalizeTransaction, under the sale row lock, on 2026-10-06.
  > consumed by: Server.SaleCommand POST /pos/sale/finalize/:id
  ~ called by: Server.SaleCommand.saleCommandServer
  ? tested by: Test.Service.SaleSpec.spec

%decision ServerOwnsMoneyAndIds
  what:    Every sale-building operation prices, taxes, computes change and generates ids on the server, then returns the whole SaleTransaction
  why:     Unit price comes from the menu (InventoryDb) at the moment of the add; taxes come from the rules in force at the sale's location at that moment. Returning the whole sale removes the client's need to refetch or merge. State guards, reservation, events and stock pulls are delegated to Service.Transaction.
  affects: startSale, addItem, addPayment, removeItem, removePayment, clear, finalize

%decision PaymentsAreApprovedOnRecord
  what:    addPayment sets paymentApproved = True and paymentAuthorizationCode = Nothing itself
  why:     There is no payment processor integration; a recorded payment is treated as taken. The request's reference text is stored in paymentReference.
  affects: addPayment

%open_issue ClearDoesNotCancelStockPulls
  what:     clear releases reservations and deletes items and payments but does not cancel the sale's stock pull requests
  why:      Same behaviour as the endpoint it replaced. removeItem does cancel pulls for its SKU.
  blocking: stockroom queue accuracy after a cleared sale
  affects:  clear

%open_issue UndecidedSaleRules
  what:     Behaviours the code currently decides by accident, awaiting an owner decision each
  why:      Price when a line grows: today the current menu price applies to every unit on the line. Which moment fixes the tax rules: today each line uses the rules at its most recent add, so two lines of one sale can differ. Overpayment: a payment may exceed what is owed and a sale may be finalized with more paid than its total; the excess is recorded nowhere. Emptied sale: clear sets Created, removing the last line leaves InProgress. Whether clear cancels stock pulls: today it does not. A maximum quantity on a line: today only the stock. Settlement: void is meant for an unsettled sale, but there is no settlement step, so a completed sale can be voided at any later time. Partial refunds and per-line restock: today a refund is the whole sale and restock is all or nothing. DECIDED between 2026-10-06 and 2026-10-08, for reference: refunded sale status is REFUNDED; no void after refund; restock on void and on refund is configuration with no default; cashiers cannot void; only the opener, a manager or an admin may write a sale; only a manager or admin may create a register (decided, not yet built).
  blocking: the formal model of the sale, a set-quantity command
  affects:  addItem, addPayment, clear, finalize

%open_issue RetriesAreNotIdempotent
  what:     A repeated add item or add payment request is applied twice
  why:      An add carries an increment, so a retry after a lost response doubles it. Planned fix: an idempotency key stored with the result inside the SQL transaction.
  blocking: safe client retries
  affects:  addItem, addPayment

%open_issue NoSetQuantityCommand
  what:     The only way to lower a line from three units to two is to remove the line and add two
  why:      Needs the same treatment as add: target quantity, stock check and repricing under the lock. Depends on the price-when-a-line-grows decision.
  blocking: cart editing
  affects:  addItem, removeItem


